15 0 obj
<< /A 38 0 R /Alt (Flowchart graphic summarizing a medical data analysis pipeline: data sources, processing and feature selection, model training \(LightGBM, Random Forest, SVM, XGBoost\), SHAP-based model interpretation, and clinical application for community validation and resource allocation.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a LASSO coefficient path plot with multiple colored lines representing feature coefficients as a function of Log\(lambda\), highlighting optimal Log\(lambda\) with a dashed line where 21 features are selected. Panel B displays a 10-fold cross-validation error plot with binomial deviance on the y-axis, Log\(lambda\) on the x-axis, red dots for mean values, gray bars for error, and the optimal Log\(lambda\) indicated by a dashed line.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Composite graphic displaying machine learning model evaluation results. Panel A shows ROC curves comparing five algorithms' performance with LightGBM achieving the highest AUC. Panel B presents corresponding precision-recall curves with LightGBM and XGBoost leading. Panel C features confusion matrices for each model, showing true and predicted classifications for two classes. Panel D displays violin plots of predicted probabilities for two patient groups across models. Panel E provides a decision curve analysis comparing net benefit against threshold probabilities for all models and baseline strategies.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Panel A displays a horizontal bar chart of SHAP global feature importance scores, ranking UAER and Course as the top predictors. Panel B shows a beeswarm summary plot of SHAP values, with feature values indicated by a blue-to-pink gradient. Panel C presents a scatter plot of SHAP values versus UAER, suggesting a strong positive relationship. Panel D provides a scatter plot of SHAP values versus Course, showing a positive correlation with increased PDR risk.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
